{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_6wzggabffgqoep7oifhregv5jainxsjcymb7xlnq34thao2r7kcq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. **The Rust translation is correct — no divergence found, so `src/` needed no changes.**\n\n## What the library is\n\n`c_src` is a single 20-line translation unit exposing exactly one symbol: `crc16` (slice-by-8 CRC-16 from tflac), plus a `static const` 8×256 table in the header.\n\n## Phases\n\n**A — Surface mapped.** `Cargo.toml` has **no `[features]`** and `CMakeLists.txt` has no options or `#ifdef`s, so the feature matrix is a single empty-feature configuration. Created `SYMBOLS.md` (1 symbol, diff empty both ways), `ERRORS.md` (8 rows), `CONFIGS.md` (20 rows). All 2048 table values verified identical by parsing both sources.\n\n**B — 20/20 `CONFIGS.md` rows pass**, including two *exhaustive* sweeps (all 65 536 seeds; all 256 byte values), block/tail path cross-checks, chained/streaming calls at aligned and unaligned splits, unaligned buffer offsets, 1 MiB buffers, and 20 000-iteration fuzz.\n\n**C — 8/8 `ERRORS.md` rows pass**, plus generic FFI boundaries. Note the C has *no* error surface at all (one `return`, no asserts, no null checks, no enums — hence no out-of-range-enum surface); `ERRORS.md` documents that derivation rather than inventing rows.\n\n**D — Symbol parity empty**, enforced by a test (not just by hand), and re-verified under the release profile (`panic = \"abort\"`) and against C built at `-O0/-O2/-O3`.\n\n## Two findings worth flagging\n\n**1. The test suite was initially vacuous — and I only caught it by mutation testing.** `cargo test` **does not build a `cdylib`**: integration tests can't link one, so Cargo never emits `libcrc16_lib.so`, and the tests silently `dlopen`ed a **stale** `.so`. My first mutation run reported all 8 mutations \"surviving\"; a deliberately broken Rust build kept passing. Fixed two ways: `run_tests.sh` always runs `cargo build` first, and `assert_fresh` in the harness panics with `STALE ARTIFACT:` if the `.so` is older than any source file. **Use `./run_tests.sh`, not bare `cargo test`.**\n\n**2. Mutation testing then confirmed real teeth: 11/11 semantic bugs killed.** One mutation survived *correctly* — raising the block threshold `len >= 8` → `len >= 16` is semantically equivalent, since slice-by-8 is a pure optimization of the byte-at-a-time tail loop (confirmed against the C itself, 500/500 cases). That's an equivalent mutant, not a blind spot.\n\nThe most interesting behavior preserved: `crc16(NULL, 0, seed) == seed` is **well-defined in C** (both loop guards fail before `d` is touched), so the Rust's `if len == 0 { return crc; }` is load-bearing — `slice::from_raw_parts(null, 0)` is UB. Removing it kills row E2 via SIGSEGV rather than a wrong value.\n\nFiles added: `tests/{common/mod.rs,differential_valid.rs,differential_errors.rs,symbol_parity.rs}`, `run_tests.sh`, `SYMBOLS.md`, `ERRORS.md`, `CONFIGS.md`, `VERIFICATION.md`. The only edit to existing files was `libloading` in `[dev-dependencies]`; `src/` and `c_src/` are byte-identical (`cmp`-verified after mutation testing)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1427,"cache_read_input_tokens":111730,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1427,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b565d8b-62d4-47a6-81b2-6a87deb725bb","uuid":"26303c75-1a02-4d29-a21b-23eef4080d26","timestamp":"2026-08-19T11:46:39.961Z"}
